+  caches take about 17.5 KiB instead of 30 KiB. The indexer's keys, the pooled blocks and the DeltaNet states stay
+  bf16. Attention reads the codes widened to bf16 exactly, so it is the bf16 kernels' arithmetic on rows rounded to
+  e4m3: lossy against a bf16 cache, deterministic for a given prompt. The MTP head's own cache stays bf16 while a
+  stream still fits the bytes it is charged (all but a stream within a twentieth of the full window;
+  `TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD_KV=fp8` keeps it fp8); on a pool's pages it is in the pages' format. It covers contiguous and
+  paged caches (`TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_PAGES`), `TF_FLASHNEXT_ATTN_LANES=1` (a round whose lanes hold one format), images
+  and video, the prompt cache and `--learn-conversations` (a kept state's head rows on disk in the format a stream
+  takes when it fits; others stay in memory). bf16 stays the default.
 - `--no-drafts` serves without the MTP head; `"draft": false` on a request does the same for that request.
 - `TF_FLASHNEXT_READOUT_ROWS` (default 64, `0` never) is the rows from which the hyper-connection read-out takes the prompt
   tiles. Same bits either way; `128` keeps 16-stream decode rounds on the row kernels, up to 7% quicker on a GB10.
